  NEW OFF-MAP TABLES (all alloc()'d, none a region):
  - THE DECLARATION-POSITION INDEX (GB-1). A type parameter in a generic
    fn's signature resolved through `_tn_resolve_at`, which scanned from
    the cursor to EOF for a later `enum` of the name (`_declared_later`)
    and walked back over every earlier fn (`_arr_fn_tparam`) — O(tokens)
    per signature, so N generic definitions cost O(N^2) (1,500 -> 3,000
    never-called `fn oK<T>(x: T)`: 400 -> 1,507 ms). `_dlx_pos` holds the
    ascending token positions of every `struct|union|enum NAME`, built
    once per token stream (keyed on GTCNT) and bisected (`_dlx_from`);
    the signature's own `<..>` is read first (`_tn_sig_tparam`). Linear.
  - THE INSTANCE CODE-RANGE STACK AND THE STACK BOUND (GB-2). A nested
    instance spent two of `_rd_enter`'s 256 nesting levels, so a 122-link
    forwarding chain was refused "over 256 levels"; behind that, each
    instance's jump targets were merged into the enclosing fn's 1023-entry
    LASE table ("function exceeds 1023 jump targets", ~190 links). Now
    `_rd_inst_enter` / `_rd_inst_exit` zero the level count for an
    instance's body and `_rd_enter` adds a STACK bound — `&m` of a local
    against the first frame it saw (`_rd_sp0`), refused past `_RD_STACK`
    = 6 MB, naming the instance count; an instance's code range goes on
    the `_jir_*` stack, inside which `IS_JUMP_TARGET` answers 1, so the
    enclosing fn's table keeps only its own targets. ~300 links compile on
    every host (cass 290). The 256-level lexical bound and its message
    are unchanged.
  - THE GVDSID METHOD-CHAIN RECORD (ZN-10). A global's call record was a
    name offset + 1. A chain ending in a method call (`R.m(..)`,
    `W.b.m(..)`, `f(..).m(..)`, `.m<..>(..)`) is now recorded TAGGED at its
    first token (`_gvd_mtag` = 2^48 + offset) and resolved lazily at the
    ask by GVDSID's one reader (`_glob_name_sid` -> `_gvm_sid` /
    `_gvm_walk`, receiver depth bounded at 8), so a method declared below
    the global counts. Read GVDSID only through `_glob_name_sid`.
  - The rest: gensig's pending-instance table (`_pn_of(sid, c0, c1)`,
    D10; lazily, as `_bnr_tab`); genbind's `**` field pin queue `_fpp` and
    rescan list `_gsl_tab`; ST-9's `_fn_rpun` byte table (alloc()'d at its
    first 1, 131,072 entries, `_fn_rps`'s convention); SS-43's
    `**S`-parameter record `_fnt_pps` (SFPPS / GFPPS, lazy at the fn cap,
    rows as `_fnt_psid`'s); FB-2r's `_gs_vkind` memo `_gvm` (256 x 48 B on
    first use); f16's `_dlvr`, `_ce_zpend`, `_dl_dv_seen`, the pre-walk's
    per-entry records and lex_pp.cyr's PP_DERIVE_CODEC / PP_DERIVE_FAM
    records (`vec_new()`'d or alloc()'d).
  THE COMMAND LINE IS READ WHOLE (TL-9). cycc, cycc_aarch64, the native
  aarch64 compiler, cycc_win's Linux arm and cycc_cx read
  /proc/self/cmdline with ONE 255-byte read into a top-level `_vbuf[256]`:
  a `--emit-js` path ending past byte 255 was cut, a flag past it dropped
  (`cycc <300-byte arg> --version` compiled its empty stdin, rc 0). One
  reader, src/common/util.cyr's `_cmdline_read()`, maps 2 MiB
  (`_cmdline_buf`), reads to EOF, and stops the compiler by name on a line
  of 2,097,152 B or more, a failed map or a failed read; `_vbuf` is its
  pointer (-2 KiB of cycc's static data). A mapping, not a top-level
  `var b[N]`: cybs sizes one as N BYTES where cycc gives N x 8, and gen1
  runs this reader. The macOS drivers (the entry stack) and cycc.exe
  (GetCommandLineW) already read the whole line.
  THE PREPROCESSOR'S WORKING MAP (TT-4). `_pp_tmp_map`
  (src/frontend/lex_pp.cyr) takes PP_IFDEF_PASS's 24 MiB buffer with
