  - THE DCE SEED PASS'S INTERVAL INDEX (IT-9). For every E8 / E9 (BL / B)
    landing on a fn start, the seed pass asked `_dce_host_fn` — a scan of
    the whole fn table — whether the site lay inside a fn: O(call sites x
    fns), on EVERY x86 / aarch64 build (the `N unreachable fns` note runs
    the walk either way). `_dce_cover_build` now packs every range
    `_dce_host_fn` tests as `start << 32 | end` once per FIXUP into an
    `alloc(fnc x 16 + 16)` buffer (the `_dce_live_starts` shape), sorts it
    (`_dce_ls_sort`), merges overlapping or touching ranges in place
    (`_dce_cover_merge`), and `_dce_in_any_fn` binary-searches the
    disjoint ranges — exact by construction; the linear scan stays as the
    fallback (a failed alloc, an end >= 2^31) and for `_dce_ev_raw` and
    the two reachable-undefined checks, which need the host's index. Both
    FIXUPs. 16,000 fns: x86 FIXUP 9,934 -> 114 ms; cycc's own `prof:
    fixup=` 820 -> 112 ms — the release's self_compile 1,190 ms (the
    gate), -34.6 % on the same input in a same-box A/B, one patch
