  - THE `**T` PIN INTERN'S HASH INDEX (VC-3). `_pp_intern` scanned every
    pin so far per `**T` annotation — quadratic once 6.7.14 raised the cap
    to 16,383. `_pp_hix` is an open-addressing index over (step word,
    field entry, struct), alloc()'d at twice `_pp_cap` slots (a power of
    two, at most half full), zeroed and rebuilt by `_pp_grow`
    (`_pp_hreindex`); the hash folds each word's high half down, because a
    step word's pin and kind sit in bits 40-61 (hashing the low bits alone
    collides). Pins keep their FIRST-COME numbers — they are baked into
    step words — so every output is byte-identical; 15,360 pins compile in
