  graph did not move cycc's own count; tests/fixtures/dead_code_floor.txt
  gains the infra lane's helpers on the forks that never call them).
  HEAP MAP: 115 regions, 0 overlaps (`sh tests/gates/memory/heapmap.sh`;
  121 through 6.7.13). THE RELEASE'S ONE HEAP-LAYOUT CHANGE IS IN-1, proven
  by the two-step bootstrap (gen1 = the slot-open cycc on the new src,
  gen1 == gen2 == gen3) before any other src/ bite branched from it: the
  six fixed IR bands are RETIRED — ir_nodes 0x5E9D000 [16 MB], ir_cp
  0x6E9D000 [4 MB], ir_blocks 0xB3A000 [4 MB], ir_state 0xF3A000 [4 KB],
  ir_live_in / ir_live_out 0x207B000 / 0x217B000 [1 MB each] — 26 MB + 4 KB
  recorded as three free gaps (0xA4A000-0x107B000, 0x207B000-0x457C000,
  whose first 4.6 MB `cx_fixup_tbl` covers on cx, and 0x5E1D000-0x7400000);
  brk-final 0xF600000 unchanged.
  THE IR ARENA (IN-1). `IR_SENABLE` takes ONE `alloc()` (`_ir_arena_init`)
  when `CYRIUS_IR` switches recording on — inside IR_SENABLE, so no driver
  can enable IR without it; a default build never takes it. The five
  tables are carved from it (nodes 16 B, node CPs 4 B, BBs 32 B, live-in
  and live-out 8 B each; bases and caps in `_ir_nodes_base`, `_ir_cp_base`,
  `_ir_ncap`, `_ir_bb_base`, `_ir_livein_base`, `_ir_liveout_base`,
  `_ir_bcap`). Initial 262,144 nodes / 32,768 BBs — small on purpose, so
  cycc's own IR build walks both grows; `_ir_nodes_grow` (nodes + CPs) and
  `_ir_bbs_grow` (BBs + live-in + live-out, one alloc) double, leaking the
  old storage as `_fixup_grow` does. The only limits are runaway ceilings,
  each named: `error: IR node table exceeds 64M nodes` (1.25 GiB),
  `error: IR block table exceeds 16M blocks` (768 MiB), and a refused
  alloc `error: cannot allocate the IR arena (CYRIUS_IR)`. The old caps
  (1,048,576 nodes / 131,072 BBs, `IR node buffer full` / `IR block table
  full`) are gone; cycc's own IR=1 self-compile had reached 654,161 nodes.
  ir_state is four globals (`_ir_ncnt`, `_ir_bcnt`, `_ir_curbb`,
  `_ir_enabled`); the accessors keep their `S` parameter.
  THE DCE REGISTRIES GROW (IN-4). WPNR (`0xC0000`) and WPSW (`0xF0000`)
  hold the FIRST 4,096 records, then `_wpnr_grow` / `_wpsw_grow` alloc a
  doubled table (WPNR's with room for `_wp_sort_prefix`'s merge scratch)
  and copy the live records, as WPJS (`0x60000`, the first 49,152) has
  since 6.6.20 — the initial regions do not move (not a layout change).
  `_wpnr_ovf` / `_wpsw_ovf` now mean only that an alloc failed; no dead-run
  count makes compaction give up. Every new DCE side table is alloc()'d on
  first use: the live-start index (IN-5), the losing-body ranges (IN-6,
  shifted by `wp_compact`, `_wp_fnr_shift`), the call-graph span map and
  the raw-asm list (IN-18), the SYMS skip bitmap (IN-8).
  THE TYPED-POINTER STEP WORD'S PIN IS RE-LAID (VC-1; 6.7.13's 7-bit pin
  capped a unit at 126 distinct `**S` pointees, a capacity regression once
  pins were keyed per struct): a pinned word is bit 62 (the "pinned" flag)
  plus a 14-bit pin in bits 48-61 (`_ps_pinned`, `_ps_pin`, `_ps_pw`) —
  free bits, because a `**T`'s pointee is a pointer and its word names no
  vector (bits 48-55 were always 0 there); `_ps_vdesc` answers 0 for a
  pinned word. So the word is: bits 0-39 the step, 40-47 the element kind,
  48-55 a `*V`'s vector descriptor less 2048 — or, with bit 62 set, 48-61
  the pin — and bit 63 CLEAR (every reader still tests `> 0`). `_pp_intern`
  holds 16,383 pins ("too many pointer-to-pointer pointee types (max
  16383)"); `_pp_tab` / `_pp_sids` start at 128 entries and double
  (`_pp_grow`); `_gv_ppn` keeps a `**T` global's pin in 16 bits (a 2 MiB
  table, alloc()'d on first use, `load16` / `store16`). The intern key
  keeps the struct. The slot mark `0 - 0x7E00 - w` still fits (the
  largest pinned word is below 2^63 - 0x7E00).
  `_lfi_base`'s per-slot value 2 (6.7.13's bare `var t: Str;` mark) is
  RETIRED (ST-12): a bare `var t: Str;` is an inline `Str` (D20 (a)), and
  `_istr_unset` / `_istr_bare` / `_istr_bare_cap` / `_istr_cpmark` are gone.
  New per-var-slot side table `_vdecl_base` (SVDECL, PL-6): the declaring
  name token's offset per var slot, alloc()'d at the var-table cap
  (1,048,576 x 4 B) like `_vecp_base`, so the native-region renumber
  warning can judge a constant where it was DECLARED; the region scanner
  is an instance (an alloc()'d state block) so the call-site and
  declaration scans do not share a cursor. Generics (no map change): every
  new or grown table is alloc()'d — `_edup`, `_bbf_vis`, `_bbf_t`, and the
  stub scan's `_gcr` / `_gsn` / `_bnr_tab` grow by doubling (`_tab_grow`;
  their 64-entry caps are gone, GN-3); the bounded-forward judgement keeps
  a 64-deep REACH cap (GN-14 — refuses a valid deeper chain; filed; FIXED
  at 6.7.15, GN-20: memoised per generic in `_bbm`, no depth cap — above).
  Backends: x86 gains `EPE_ERRNO_STUBS` (PL-1): the PE `GetLastError` →
  negative-errno table is emitted ONCE after EEXIT by every x86 driver,
  beside EMACHO_SYSX_STUBS; each reroute site is a 13-byte `call .`
  placeholder registered in WPJS (`_wpjs_add_raw`, so compaction moves it)
  and FIXUP asserts every placeholder patched (`_pew_stubs_drained`) —
  +13,824 B on cycc_win.exe where a per-site table was +156,672 B. The
  arm64 Mach-O at-rows all keep x0 (`_esx_arm_atfd`; the arg-shift emitter
  `_esx_arm_shift` is REMOVED, PL-5). cycc_cx (not cycc): every patchable
  `jz` / `jnz` is the inverted short branch over a 24-bit `jmp` (+4 B a
  conditional, LIB-1). IR opcode set: UNCHANGED (IN-2's narrow-field loads
  and ST-1's float literal record `IR_RAW_EMIT`). Hidden temps
  (`hidden_temp_census.sh`): 36 `_HTEMP(S)` call sites — `_istr_rax_into`
  (ST-12) and `_dvi_park` (VC-13) new, `_ret_addr_field` renamed
  `_ret_park_copy` (ST-11), `_vrcv_demit` renamed `_vrcv_dparse` (VC-13).
  cybs (IN-10 - IN-12): labels 508 / 512, input 119,157 / 131,072 B, code
  22,890 / 65,536 B (the seed-assembled cybs 23,010 B); its preprocessor
  caps are refused by name — 15 MB stdin, a 2 MB slot per include depth
  (`r15 + 0x9000000 + depth x 2 MB`), 8 depths, a 16 MB expansion.
  Modules: 32 (unchanged). Corpus: 642 .tcyr (335 in crossos/), 550 shell
  gates (check.sh 554 / 554 on the wave-3 merge, the driver 131 / 131),
  api-surface 5,891.

