== HEAP MAP: 102 REGIONS, 0 OVERLAPS ==

`sh tests/gates/memory/heapmap.sh` (the path moved in the v6.5.11
reorg; this entry said `tests/heapmap.sh`) parses the authoritative heap map out of the
`#   0xOFFSET  name  [BYTES]` comment block at the top of src/main.cyr —
one "region" per such line — sorts them and reports any pair whose
[base, base+size) ranges intersect. It is a MAP audit, not a runtime
audit: it proves the documented layout is self-consistent, not that
code writes where the map says (v6.4.81 found a smashed scratch buffer
documented at an address no code had ever written).

The count went 100 (through 6.4.74) → 94 (at .75, when six fn-indexed
side tables moved to lazy alloc and their offsets became FREED markers)
→ 100 again (at .81, when the auditor's size parser was fixed to see
unit-suffixed entries it had been silently dropping). Same number by a
DIFFERENT route — the pre-.75 100 and today's 100 are not the same set.

It held at 100 across most of v6.5.x and is **102 since v6.6.1**
(unchanged at 6.6.19 / 6.6.20: `heapmap.sh` → 102 regions, 0 warnings) — and the
stability is NOT an accident: v6.5.0's two visibility side tables
deliberately lazy-alloc at their table's max cap instead of taking a heap
band, so they add no map line, no layout change, and therefore no two-step
bootstrap. That is now the default shape for a new fn- or vcnt-indexed
table (see the exhaustive_match entry's CURRENCY note).

⚠ THE 102 ABOVE IS THE 6.6.19 SNAPSHOT. The v6.7.x minor took the count to
123 (6.7.10 / 6.7.11), 121 (6.7.12: cx's two fixed regions FREED) and
**115 at 6.7.14**: the six IR bands (ir_nodes, ir_cp, ir_blocks, ir_state,
ir_live_in, ir_live_out) were RETIRED when the IR became one alloc()'d
arena (IN-1 — that release's one heap-layout change, a two-step
bootstrap) — and still **115 at 6.7.15**, which changed no layout (its
one map-row edit, include_fnames at 0x1C0000, keeps its bounds and now
holds pointers, IT-5), and at **6.7.16**, which touched no map row. See
the DELTAS blocks above; derive the live number with the gate.

== GROWABLE TABLE CAPS ==

Four families are grow-on-demand; the heap-map offset is the INITIAL
base, valid only under the first cap. (6.6.19 snapshot. Since then: the
IR arena — no map region at all since 6.7.14, 262,144 nodes / 32,768 BBs
initial, doubling, runaway ceilings 64M nodes / 16M BBs; the DCE
registries WPNR `0xC0000` / WPSW `0xF0000`, the first 4,096 records then
alloc()'d and doubling since 6.7.14, as WPJS `0x60000` past 49,152 since
6.6.20; the `**T` pin table `_pp_tab`, 128 entries doubling to 16,383
pins since 6.7.14 — the 6.7.14 DELTAS block above has each — with its
hash index `_pp_hix` at twice the cap, rebuilt on each grow, since 6.7.15;
the bounded-forward memo `_bbm` and the DCE seed pass's interval index,
alloc()'d since 6.7.15 — the 6.7.15 DELTAS block; 6.7.16's tables are all
alloc()'d on first use or lazily at the fn cap, none a region — the 6.7.16
DELTAS block lists them.)

  fn table       init 2048 (`_fnt_cap`, v6.5.51 — half the fixed
                 4096-slot hash regions; was 4096 from v6.5.40, 8192
                 before), `_fnt_grow` doubles,
                 CEILING 131072
                 (v6.5.40 raised it from 32768; the old "2-byte hash
                 slots store fi+1, so fi+1 <= 65535" rationale below is
                 HISTORY — the slots were widened, which is what let the
                 ceiling move).
                 ⚠ v6.5.46: raising that ceiling did NOT sweep its
                 consumers — the DCE reachability bitmap `live[]` was
                 widened to 16384 bytes but its clear loop stayed at
                 4096 and the address-taken root-seed bound at 32768,
                 so `CYRIUS_DCE=1` NOP-filled any address-taken fn above
                 index 32768 (measured: SIGSEGV on a 33,001-fn program).
                 Both bounds are now DERIVED from the ceiling and gated.
                 The capacity warning fires at 85% of the ceiling (v6.4.75 —
                 it used to divide by the LIVE cap, so it screamed at
                 8191 and went silent the instant the table grew).
                 Six fn-indexed SIDE tables (fn_deprecated_msg,
                 fn_regalloc, fn_ret_sid, fn_variadic, fn_flags,
                 fn_var_bytes) were left behind at fixed 8192-slot bands
                 by the v6.2.0 migration — index 8192 aliased index 0 of
                 the neighbour. v6.4.75 gave each a lazy alloc on first
                 write, so they can never desync the grow chain; today
                 they are `alloc(131072*8)`, sized to the ceiling.

  var family     7 vcnt-indexed parallel tables (var_noffs, var_sizes,
                 var_types, gvar_byte_off, enum_const_val, gvar_initval,
                 var_enum_id). init 8192, `_var_grow` doubles, hard error
                 at 1,048,576 entries. v6.3.0.

  fixup table    0x107B000, 1,048,576 entries x 16 bytes = 16 MB init;
                 `_fixup_base` / `_fixup_cap` relocate + double (v6.2.0)
                 to a runaway ceiling of 67,108,864 entries (64M = 1 GiB).
                 ⚠ The 85 % capacity warning still divides by 1,048,576,
                 the INITIAL cap, not the ceiling.

  codebuf        off-heap `alloc(8388608)` (8 MiB) on the six native
                 forks, growing in +8 MiB LINEAR steps (v6.4.49; was 2x)
                 to a 64 MiB ceiling (`_codebuf_grow`). The cx backend's
                 OWN code region is the exception — since 6.7.12
                 `_cx_code_base`, a FIXED off-heap `alloc(4194304)`
                 (4 MiB, `_CX_CODE_CAP`) that never grows and is refused
                 by name past it, with its break-chain shadow an
                 `alloc(cap + 8)` in `_codebuf_base`; since 6.7.14 a cx
                 conditional reaches the whole region (an inverted
                 short branch over a 24-bit `jmp`, LIB-1 — a `jz` /
                 `jnz` over 128 KiB wrapped silently before). Until 6.7.12 it
                 was a FIXED 512 KiB at 0x54A000 (cx_codebuf) with the
                 shadow at 0x41A000 [3 MB] (cx_brk_shadow, the pre-.49
                 codebuf base) — both heap-map regions are FREED.

== FIXED CAPS ==

  preprocessed source          24 MB (`_SRC_CAP` = 25165824, `_SRCB` at
                               0x7400000) since v6.5.40; was a FIXED
                               8 MB slot whose overflow was a hard build
                               failure with no flag, no env var and no
                               manifest key — a project that hit it had
                               exactly one move, hand-vendoring a subset
                               of its dependencies. ⭐ Raising it exposed
                               FOUR more caps in turn (tokens, the
                               identifier pool, the fn table, and the
                               identifier-dedup table); fixing only the
                               filed one would have moved the usable
                               ceiling 8 MB -> ~10-11 MB and been
                               reported as 3x. PP_IFDEF_PASS's own
                               24 MiB working map (`_pp_tmp_map`) is
                               refused by name when the map fails since
                               6.7.16 (TT-4; it was written through).

  command line (/proc drivers) 2 MiB, read whole (`_cmdline_read`; a line
                               of 2,097,152 B or more refused by name)
                               since 6.7.16 (TL-9) — one 255-byte read
                               before, cut silently past it.
  nesting                      256 levels of lexical nesting (`_rd_enter`,
                               "nesting too deep"); since 6.7.16 a generic
                               instance's body restarts the count and
                               instance nesting is bounded by 6 MB of the
                               compiler's stack (`_RD_STACK`, GB-2) —
                               ~300 forwarding links.

  identifier pool (tok_names)  8 MB at 0xEC00000 since v6.5.40 (was
                               512 KB at 0x60000-0xE0000 at v6.4.76, and
                               256 KB before that). LEX refuses past
                               8388336, leaving 272 B of slack for the
                               inner write loop. ⚠ The old note that the
                               pool END must stay <= 0x100000 or the
                               compiler HANGS applied to the 0x60000
                               placement and is HISTORY — v6.5.40 moved
                               the pool out of that band entirely as one
                               of the four caps stacked behind the
                               preprocess ceiling.
  tokens                       4,194,304 slots (v6.5.39; was 1,048,576)
                               each for tok_types /
                               tok_values / tok_lines (32 MB apiece —
                               4,194,304 x 8 bytes; the heap map said
                               8 MB for tok_values until v6.5.46, a
                               one-line omission in the three-line
                               v6.5.39 resize that made the machine-read
                               auditor report 24 MB of free band which
                               is fully occupied).
                               Since v6.4.60 tok_lines packs the token
                               BYTE OFFSET into its high 32 bits — that
                               is where column + caret diagnostics come
                               from, at zero new heap.
  struct ids                   1024 (struct_names at 0x1A6018). This is
                               the cap the `<= -2048` SIMD descriptor
                               band must be guarded against — see the
                               type_id_encoding entry.
  enums                        1024 enum decls, 1024 per-enum variant
                               counts (v5.8.24; stdlib alone was at 299).
  input_buf                    24 MB at 0x7400000 (`_SRCB`, v6.5.39) —
                               raw stdin + the preprocessor's working
                               buffer; its cap must equal preprocess_out's.
  output image                 NOT a heap region any more: an off-heap,
                               lazily-mapped `alloc(1073741824)` (1 GiB,
                               `_output_base` / `_output_cap`) on the six
                               native drivers since v6.4.51/.52 (cx emits
                               .cyx and has no output image). The in-heap
                               16 MB output_buf band is retired.
  string data                  2 MiB (2,097,152 B; warns at 85 %).
  string-intern index          6.6.19 (B0b): a lazily `alloc`'d FNV-1a
                               index over the pool's segments — off the
                               map, adds no region.

== IR OPCODE SET (src/common/ir.cyr, `enum IROp`) ==

65 opcodes, numbered 0..101 with deliberate gaps so a class can grow
without renumbering:

  0-9    values      NOP, LOAD_IMM, LOAD/STORE_LOCAL, LOAD/STORE_GLOBAL,
                     LOAD_ADDR_L/_G, LOAD_STR, LOAD_ADDR_G_X1
  10-15  arithmetic  ADD SUB MUL DIV MOD NEG
  20-26  bitwise     AND OR XOR NOT SHL SHR ASHR
                     (SHR is LOGICAL, ASHR is `>>>` — the reverse of
                     JS/Java; never flip it)
  30-33  stack       PUSH, POP_RAX, POP_RCX, MOV_CA
  40-47  memory      LOAD8/16/32/64, STORE8/16/32/64
  50-52  compare     CMP, SETCC, TEST_AZ
  60-66  calls       CALL, CALL_KNOWN, CALL_POPS, CALL_CLEAN, TAIL_JMP,
                     SYSCALL, CALL_INDIRECT
  70-74  control     JMP, JCC, RET, JMP_BACK, SWITCH
  80-83  frame       PROLOGUE, ALLOC_FRAME, EPILOGUE, PATCH_FRAME
  90-99  misc        RAW_BYTE, MOV_RDX_RAX, MOV_RAX_RDX, XOR_AA,
                     STORE_PARM, ADD_IMM_X1, RAX_CLOBBER, RAW_EMIT,
                     ELIMINATED (LASE-eliminated, NOP-filled)
  100-101            MOV_R3_RAX / MOV_RAX_R3 (three-value returns,
                     v6.5.21)

Unchanged through 6.7.16. An emitter with no opcode of its own records
RAW_EMIT — every one must record SOMETHING, because IR=3's passes
NOP-fill a node's range up to the next node's cp, so unrecorded bytes
belong to the node before them (6.7.14: the narrow-field `movsx` IN-2,
the float literal's `movabs` ST-1). The converse holds too (6.7.15,
IT-1): a pass that rewrites a byte span must consume every node inside
it — `ir_const_fold` left an IR_ELIMINATED dead store in its span, and
the deferred NOP fill landed in the folded `mov eax, imm32`
(`_ir_fold_consume_span`). Its STORAGE changed in 6.7.14: one alloc()'d
arena, not six heap bands (the DELTAS block above).

== BACKEND MODULES (src/backend/) ==

  x86/       emit.cyr, jump.cyr, fixup.cyr, decode.cyr (length-decoder),
             float.cyr — SSE/AVX scalar FP **and ALL SIMD emitters**,
             including the first VEX-encoding emitters the toolchain
             ever had (the v6.4.x arc)
  aarch64/   emit.cyr, jump.cyr, fixup.cyr (NEON SIMD lives in emit.cyr)
  cx/        emit.cyr — cyrius-x portable bytecode; runner is
             programs/cxvm.cyr
  js/        emit.cyr — TS/TSX -> JS (`cycc --emit-js`; in every fork
             but cx since 6.7.15, PL-13 — main.cyr alone before)
  macho/     emit.cyr — Mach-O container (arm64 + x86_64)
  pe/        emit.cyr — Windows PE container
  common/    env.cyr (the env reader shared by every fork incl. cx,
             6.6.10), runtime.cyr, tokens.cyr — shared across every fork
  plus src/common/syscall_xlat.cyr — GENERATED by
  programs/gen_syscall_xlat.cyr from the two Linux syscall tables,
  gated by tests/gates/platform/syscall_xlat_generated.sh (since
  6.7.12 it also generates `_SYSX_A64(n)`, the aarch64 names the
  native-region renumber warning prints); x86/emit.cyr holds
  `EMACHO_SYSX_STUBS` since 6.7.12 (the x86 Mach-O run-time-number
  stubs, called by every x86 driver between EEXIT and FIXUP) and
  `EPE_ERRNO_STUBS` since 6.7.14 (the PE GetLastError → errno table,
  emitted once beside them; FIXUP asserts every `call .` site patched;
  stub classes 2 / 3, the std close and the seek check, since 6.7.16),
  with the PE reroutes' shared BOOL → 0 / -errno fold `_pe_bool_errno`
  and the fd low-bit guard's tail `_pe_fd_bad_tail` since 6.7.16

== PER-TARGET FORKS: 7 ==

  src/main.cyr                  x86_64 Linux (also drives macho/pe/js)
  src/main_aarch64.cyr          x86-hosted aarch64 cross
  src/main_aarch64_macho.cyr    macOS arm64
  src/main_aarch64_native.cyr   aarch64-hosted native
  src/main_win.cyr              Windows PE
  src/main_x86_macho.cyr        Intel-Mac x86_64 Mach-O
  src/main_cx.cyr               cx bytecode

plus src/version_str.cyr (generated by version-bump.sh). Since 6.7.15
(PL-13, D38) the six host forks all carry the TypeScript front end
(`--lex-ts` / `--parse-ts` / `--emit-js`) through the shared
src/frontend/ts/driver*.cyr includes — before, every fork but main.cyr
skipped those flags like any unknown one and compiled the TypeScript as
cyrius; main_cx.cyr still has none. Since 6.7.16 all seven read
CYRIUS_MONOMORPH before pass 1 (FF-50) and the five /proc drivers read
the whole command line through one reader (TL-9) — the 6.7.16 DELTAS
block.

WHY 7 FORKS MATTER TO TYPE WORK: a new type-system feature that touches
codegen has to be added to the emitters of every fork that can reach it,
and a fork that only ever gets a return-0 stub will compile and pass
tests while silently emitting nothing. The v6.4.26 trap: a new PE-only
reroute needed return-0 stubs in the aarch64 AND cx forks, and only the
cx build on real Windows hardware caught the miss.
